        'Dashboard' => [
            'body' => '<p>The IFRS 9 ECL Dashboard is the one-page position of the loan book for a reporting period: how much is exposed, how much ECL is held against it and on which basis, how the book splits across the three IFRS 9 stages, where the ECL sits, how it has moved over the months, what it would be under each economic scenario, and how often loans have actually defaulted. It is the landing page after sign-in and is read by management, finance and risk staff. Anyone who can sign in can open it; nothing on it changes data. To return to it, press <b>Dashboard</b> at the top of the sidebar or the logo. Every figure is read from the saved ECL runs and loan books for the period, portfolio and comparison month you choose; only months for which ECL has been calculated are offered.</p>'
                . '<h4>What you see on the screen</h4><ul>'
                . '<li><b>Heading</b>: <b>IFRS 9 ECL Dashboard</b> with the small round green help button beside it, and a line such as <b>Showing Nov 2025</b>, followed by <b>portfolio</b> and its name when one is chosen and <b>compared with Oct 2025</b> when there is a comparison month.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Filter bar</b> (a green panel in the actions row above the tiles) with three drop-downs: <b>Reporting period</b> (newest first; the latest calculated month is chosen by default), <b>Portfolio</b> (<b>All portfolios</b> or one loan portfolio) and <b>Compare to</b> (<b>Previous period</b>, meaning the closest earlier calculated month, or any earlier calculated month). Changing any of them reloads the whole page. Beside it the gold <b>PDF</b> button.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Six KPI tiles</b>, each a white card with a coloured left edge, an icon, a label, a compact value (for example <code>MWK 384.45M</code>), the exact amount in small grey text and either a change chip or a note: <b>Total exposure (EAD)</b>; <b>Total ECL (booked)</b> or <b>Total ECL (undiscounted)</b>; <b>ECL coverage</b>; <b>Stage 3 exposure</b>; <b>Weighted PD</b>; <b>Weighted LGD</b>. Hover a tile for the full figure.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Three stage cards</b>: <b>Stage 1</b> (green, badge <b>Performing</b>), <b>Stage 2</b> (amber, badge <b>Under-performing</b>) and <b>Stage 3</b> (red, badge <b>Credit-impaired</b>). Each shows <b>Exposure (EAD)</b> in large type, then <b>ECL</b>, <b>Coverage</b>, <b>PD applied</b>, <b>LGD applied</b>, <b>Loans</b> and <b>Share of book</b>.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Exposure by stage</b>: a doughnut of the EAD in each stage, with a <b>Chart</b> / <b>Table</b> toggle. Hovering a segment shows its amount, its share and the number of loans. The table has <b>Stage</b>, <b>EAD</b> and <b>Share</b>.</li>'
                . '<li><b>ECL and coverage trend</b>: stacked bars of <b>Stage 1 ECL</b>, <b>Stage 2 ECL</b> and <b>Stage 3 ECL</b> per month (left scale), the <b>Coverage %</b> line above them (right scale; the reporting month is marked with a larger gold dot) and the <b>Exposure (EAD)</b> as a dashed grey shaded line behind them. Its own two range drop-downs (see Filters), a <b>Chart</b> / <b>Table</b> toggle and a caption giving the months shown. The table has <b>Period</b>, <b>EAD</b>, <b>ECL</b> and <b>Coverage</b>.</li>'
                . '<li><b>ECL build-up</b>: how the ECL of the month is built, as a small waterfall of bars: <b>ECL before FLI</b> (EAD x PD before FLI over the horizon x LGD), <b>Forward-looking effect</b> (the macro adjustment to the PD, weighted across the scenario set), <b>Manual overlays</b> (the approved overlays from the register, or <b>No approved overlay applied to these loans</b>), <b>Mega Farm programme</b> (only when the month holds programme loans, measured by the programme engine) and <b>ECL booked</b>. Each movement shows its percentage of the ECL before FLI. A badge reads <b>Ties to the total ECL</b> (green) or <b>Differs from the saved runs</b> (amber; hover for the saved total). A last line reads <b>Ran under</b> the route, the regression fit and the scenario set the month used.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Where the ECL sits</b>: the ECL split by <b>Product group</b>, <b>Sector</b> or <b>RBM class</b> (a three-way switch), with a <b>Chart</b> / <b>Table</b> toggle; it opens on the table. Product group and sector show the six largest by ECL and the rest as one line in grey italics; RBM class shows the Reserve Bank of Malawi classes. The table has the dimension, <b>Loans</b>, <b>EAD</b>, <b>ECL</b>, <b>Coverage</b>, on the RBM view <b>RBM min.</b> (the directive\'s minimum provision for the class), and <b>Share</b> (a small green bar and the percentage of the total ECL). The <b>Total</b> row ends with <b>100%, ties</b> (green) when it agrees with the Total ECL tile, or <b>Differs</b> (amber). The chart draws green horizontal bars of ECL, the coverage as diamond markers on the top scale and, on the RBM view, the RBM minimum as gold markers.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Portfolio summary</b>: a table with the note <b>Values in MWK</b> (your organisation currency). Columns: <b>Metric</b>, the reporting month, and, when there is a comparison month, that month, <b>Change</b> and <b>Status</b>. Rows: <b>Number of loans</b>, <b>Total EAD</b>, <b>Stage 3 share of book</b>, <b>Weighted PD</b>, <b>Weighted LGD</b>, <b>ECL coverage</b>, <b>Total ECL</b> and <b>Net carrying amount</b>.</li>'
                . '<li><b>ECL by portfolio over months</b> (titled <b>ECL by product group over months</b> when one portfolio is chosen): one line per portfolio (or product group), the six largest in the last month of the range and the rest as one dashed grey line <b>Other (n)</b>. Its own range drop-downs, a badge <b>Each month ties to the total ECL</b> (green) or <b>Differs from the total ECL in N months</b> (amber, hover for the months and amounts), and a <b>Chart</b> / <b>Table</b> toggle. The table has <b>Period</b>, one column per line and <b>Total</b>. Hovering a month lists every line, largest first, with the total ECL as the footer.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Base and stressed ECL</b>: bars of the ECL of each month under each scenario of the scenario set in force (<b>Upside</b>, <b>Base</b>, <b>Downside</b>, <b>Severe</b>, each with its weight, for example <b>Base (50%)</b>), with the <b>Probability-weighted</b> ECL drawn as a trend line across them (it is the blend of the scenarios, not one of them). Its own range drop-downs, a stage drop-down (<b>All stages</b>, <b>Stage 1</b>, <b>Stage 2</b>, <b>Stage 3</b>), a <b>Chart</b> / <b>Table</b> toggle and a badge <b>Weighted ties to the total ECL</b> (green) or <b>Differs from the total ECL in N periods</b> (amber). The table has <b>Period</b>, one column per scenario and <b>Loans</b>. Under it, amber lines carry any note. Where each month came from (its forward-looking month-end record or the saved stress runs) and who approved the scenario set are shown on the Stress Testing and Scenario Sets screens, not on the dashboard (removed 15 October 2026).</li>'
                . '<li><b>Observed default rate</b>: the share of the Stage 1 and 2 balance that defaulted or left the book unpaid, as lines: <b>Whole book, month</b> (solid) and <b>Whole book, 12 months</b> (dashed), plus the same two lines for the chosen portfolio. Its own range drop-downs and a <b>Chart</b> / <b>Table</b> toggle. The table has <b>Period</b>, <b>Book, month</b>, <b>Book, 12 months</b> and, with a portfolio chosen, <b>Portfolio, month</b> and <b>Portfolio, 12 months</b>; each cell reads for example <code>1.25% (12 of 960)</code> and hovering gives the balances. A note explains the measure; amber lines start <b>Not measured:</b>.</li></ul>'
                . '<h4>What each tile means</h4><ul>'
                . '<li><b>Total exposure (EAD)</b>: the exposure the ECL engine measured: the carrying amount of every loan plus the drawn share of undrawn commitments, for the month and portfolio.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Total ECL (booked)</b>: the ECL discounted at the effective interest rate, which is the allowance that is booked. It is shown only when every ECL run of the month (and of the comparison month) was discounted; the small text reads <b>, discounted at the EIR</b>. Otherwise the tile is <b>Total ECL (undiscounted)</b> and the small text says <b>the period was run undiscounted</b>, so the two bases are never mixed.</li>'
                . '<li><b>ECL coverage</b>: Total ECL divided by Total exposure, as a percentage.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Stage 3 exposure</b>: the exposure of loans whose final stage (after qualitative overrides) is Stage 3; when there is no change chip the note gives its share of the book.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Weighted PD</b> and <b>Weighted LGD</b>: the average PD and LGD the ECL run used in each stage, weighted by each stage\'s exposure across all three stages.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Net carrying amount</b> (summary table only): the gross carrying amount of the book less the Total ECL.</li></ul>'
                . '<h4>Change chips and status</h4><p>With a comparison month, each money tile shows a chip such as <b>+3.2% vs Oct 2025</b> and each ratio tile a chip in points such as <b>-0.15pts vs Oct 2025</b>, with a small up or down triangle. The colour reads the business meaning, not the direction: more exposure is green, while a rise in ECL, coverage, Stage 3 exposure, PD or LGD is red. A grey chip means no material change; no chip appears when the earlier value is zero. In the <b>Portfolio summary</b> the <b>Status</b> column grades each row: a move in the favourable direction is <b>Favourable</b> (green); an adverse move under 10% (or under 1 point for a ratio) is <b>Watch</b> (gold); a larger adverse move is <b>Adverse</b> (red); a move under 1% (or under 0.05 points) is <b>Stable</b> (grey).</p>'
                . '<h4>Buttons and icons</h4><ul>'
                . '<li><b>Help button</b> (green question mark beside the title): opens this article.</li>'
                . '<li><b>PDF</b> (gold, document icon): downloads the dashboard for the chosen period, portfolio and comparison month as a branded A4 PDF with the same figures, the stage mix and trend drawn on the server, the portfolio summary and the month-end status. Any signed-in user may download it.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Chart</b> / <b>Table</b>: switches a panel between the picture and its figures; the green half is the view shown. The choice is not remembered when the page reloads.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Product group</b> / <b>Sector</b> / <b>RBM class</b>: chooses the split of Where the ECL sits.</li>'
