                . '<h4>Filters and exports</h4><p>The filter bar scopes the whole page. Each trend chart also has its own range: a <b>From</b> drop-down (<b>Last 12 months</b>, the default, <b>From the start</b>, or <b>From</b> any calculated month) and a <b>To</b> drop-down (<b>To</b> the reporting month, the default, or any calculated month). Changing the range of ECL and coverage trend reloads the page; changing the range of the three charts lower down reloads only that chart and keeps your place. Only months that really exist are plotted; nothing is filled with zeros. All choices are carried in the page address, so a view can be bookmarked or shared. The <b>PDF</b> button exports what the filter bar shows.</p>'
                . '<h4>To compare two months</h4><ol><li>Choose the later month in <b>Reporting period</b>.</li><li>Choose the earlier month in <b>Compare to</b>, or leave <b>Previous period</b>. Only months before the reporting month are listed; if you move the reporting month to or before the comparison month, the closest earlier month is used instead.</li><li>Read the chips on the tiles and the <b>Change</b> and <b>Status</b> columns of the Portfolio summary.</li></ol>'
                . '<h4>To see where the ECL moved</h4><ol><li>Read the <b>ECL build-up</b> for the effect of the forward-looking adjustment and the overlays.</li><li>Switch <b>Where the ECL sits</b> between Product group, Sector and RBM class, and press <b>Chart</b> for the picture.</li><li>Widen the range of <b>ECL by portfolio over months</b> with its <b>From</b> drop-down to see which portfolio drove the change.</li></ol>'
                . '<h4>What happens next</h4><p>The Dashboard is read-only. It shows whatever the last ECL calculation, forward-looking month-end and stress runs saved for the month, so when a run is repeated the figures change the next time the page loads.</p>'
                . '<h4>Empty states and messages</h4><ul>'
