        'Period Workspace' => [
            'body' => '<p>The Workspace tracks the month-end IFRS 9 close of one reporting period as a ten-step checklist, lists everything across the system that is waiting for a second person to approve, and keeps the team\'s notes about the period in one place. Analysts use it to see what is still outstanding and where to do it; reviewers use it to find what waits for their approval; administrators tick the two steps that need human judgement. Everyone who can sign in can open it. To reach it, press <b>Workspace</b> at the top of the sidebar; the breadcrumb reads <b>Workspace</b>.</p>'
                . '<h4>What you see on the screen</h4><ul>'
                . '<li>Title <b>Workspace</b> and the line <b>The month-end IFRS 9 close for one reporting period: each step, who did it, and the team\'s notes</b>.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Reporting period</b> drop-down (in the actions row at the right): every month that has a loan book, newest first, written as year and month (for example <code>2025-11</code>). Changing it reloads the checklist for that month.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Four tiles</b>: <b>Close progress</b> with the month, a percentage and a green progress bar; <b>Steps done</b> (for example <b>7 of 10</b>); <b>Outstanding</b> (the number of steps not done, amber when above zero; hover for their names); <b>Signed in as</b> with your name (hover for your email) and either <b>Administrator: can tick manual steps</b> or <b>Read-only view</b>.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Three tabs</b>, each with a count chip: <b>IFRS 9 close checklist</b> (for example <b>7/10</b>), <b>Awaiting approval</b> (the total number of items waiting) and <b>Team messages</b> (the number of messages shown).</li>'
                . '<li>On the checklist tab a grey line reads <b>Steps marked System are checked automatically from the data; an administrator ticks the others.</b> followed by <b>Still to do:</b> and the outstanding step names in amber, or <b>All steps complete for this period.</b> in green.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Checklist rows</b>, one per step: a numbered circle (a white tick on green once done), the step name (struck through once done), a grey detail line, and at the right a grey <b>System</b> badge with a padlock on system-verified steps (hover: <b>Verified automatically from the database</b>), a <b>Done</b> (solid green) or <b>Pending</b> (gold) badge, a green arrow button and, for administrators on the two manual steps only, a tick or circular-arrow button.</li></ul>'
                . '<h4>The ten steps</h4><ol>'
                . '<li><b>Import the loan book for the period</b> (System): done when the month has loan book rows. Detail: for example <b>3,593 loans imported</b>, or <b>No loan book rows for this period</b>. The arrow opens Imports.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Portfolio segmentation &amp; sector tags</b> (System): done when every loan has a portfolio. Detail: <b>3,593 of 3,593 loans assigned to a portfolio</b>. Opens Loan Portfolios.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Stage allocation (SICR rules applied)</b> (System): done when every loan has a final stage. Detail: <b>N of N loans staged</b>. Opens Settings on the Staging basis tab.</li>'
                . '<li><b>PD model applied to the loan book</b> (System): done when at least one loan carries a PD (before or after the forward-looking adjustment). Detail: <b>N loans carry a PD</b>. Opens Monthly Probability.</li>'
                . '<li><b>LGD model applied to the loan book</b> (System): done when at least one loan carries an LGD. Detail: <b>N loans carry an LGD</b>. Opens Monthly LGD.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Forward-looking month-end (route, record, sign-off)</b> (System): done only when the FLI month-end is complete: the forward-looking route applied to every loan under the model version and scenario set in force, the ECL calculated after it, and the month recorded and signed off by a second person. The detail repeats the FLI Overview\'s status, for example <b>Route applied; record the month: ...</b> or <b>Signed off by</b> a name and date. Opens FLI Month-End, Overview.</li>'
                . '<li><b>ECL calculation run</b> (System): done when ECL result rows exist for the month. Detail: <b>N ECL result rows</b> or <b>ECL not calculated for this period</b>. Opens ECL Calculation.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Review IFRS 9 reports &amp; data quality</b> (manual): ticked by an administrator after the review. Opens the Reports hub.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Stress / sensitivity scenarios run</b> (System): done when a stress scenario run is saved for the month. Detail: <b>N saved scenario run(s)</b> or <b>No saved stress scenarios</b>. Opens Stress Testing.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Management sign-off for the period</b> (manual): ticked by an administrator when management has signed the month off. It has no linked screen.</li></ol>'
                . '<p>System steps are worked out from the database every time the page loads and can never be ticked by hand. Steps 2 to 6 read <b>Awaiting loan book</b> until step 1 is done. A manual step shows <b>Ticked by</b> the name and the date and time once done. The month-end job on Maintenance (<b>Run the month-end calculations</b>) runs the staging, PD and LGD, forward-looking route, ECL and month record steps in order; the checklist turns green by itself as their results are saved.</p>'
                . '<h4>The Awaiting approval tab</h4><p>A grey line reads <b>Everything a second person must approve, across the system (all periods). The person who proposed an item cannot approve it.</b> Each line has a gold count badge, the name of what waits and a green arrow (<b>Open:</b> and the name) to the screen where it is approved. Only lines with something waiting are listed:</p><ul>'
