                . '<li><b>Grey circular arrow</b> (<b>Reopen this step</b>): sets a done manual step back to pending. Administrators only.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Green arrow</b> on an Awaiting approval line: opens the screen that holds those items.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Send</b>: posts your message to everyone. It is greyed until the box holds text. The Enter key sends; Shift with Enter starts a new line.</li></ul>'
                . '<h4>To tick a manual step (administrators)</h4><ol><li>Choose the month in <b>Reporting period</b>.</li><li>On <b>Review IFRS 9 reports &amp; data quality</b> or <b>Management sign-off for the period</b> press the gold tick (<b>Mark as done</b>).</li><li>A green message confirms, for example <b>Step "Management sign-off for the period" completed for 2025-11.</b></li><li>To undo, press the grey circular arrow (<b>Reopen this step</b>); the message then ends <b>reopened for 2025-11.</b></li></ol>'
                . '<h4>To clear what waits for approval</h4><ol><li>Open the <b>Awaiting approval</b> tab.</li><li>Press the green arrow on a line to open its screen.</li><li>Review and approve or reject each item there. If you proposed an item, ask a colleague to approve it.</li></ol>'
                . '<h4>To post a team message</h4><ol><li>Open the <b>Team messages</b> tab.</li><li>Type in the box (up to 2,000 characters) and press <b>Send</b> or Enter.</li></ol>'
                . '<h4>What happens next</h4><p>Ticking or reopening a manual step is stored against the month with your name and the time, and every other administrator receives a bell notification such as <b>Jane Phiri completed "Management sign-off for the period" for 2025-11.</b> that links back to this page. Messages are visible to everyone signed in. Nothing in the Workspace changes loan data; it records and shows the state of the close. The Workspace does not lock the month: a reporting period is locked on Imports &amp; Feeds, Periods Built, once its month-end is signed off.</p>'
                . '<h4>Empty states and messages</h4><ul><li><b>Nothing is waiting for approval.</b> (Awaiting approval tab).</li><li><b>No messages yet. Start the conversation for this period.</b> (Team messages tab).</li><li><b>Only administrators can update the workspace.</b> appears as a <b>No access rights</b> dialogue if a user without the administrator role tries to tick a step.</li><li><b>This step is verified automatically by the system.</b> A System step cannot be ticked; do the work on the linked screen.</li></ul>'
                . '<h4>Common problems</h4><ul><li><b>The tick buttons are missing.</b> Only users with the administrator role can tick; your tile reads <b>Read-only view</b>.</li><li><b>The month I need is not listed.</b> The list holds months that have a loan book; build or import it first.</li><li><b>Step 6 stays Pending although the ECL ran.</b> The forward-looking month must also be recorded and signed off by a second person on FLI Month-End, Overview, after the ECL.</li><li><b>An Awaiting approval line will not clear.</b> You are the proposer of those items; a different person must approve them.</li></ul>',
            'steps' => [
                'Press Workspace at the top of the sidebar and choose the month in Reporting period.',
                'Read the four tiles and the Still to do line to see what is outstanding.',
                'On a Pending row press the green arrow (Open this screen) and do the step there; System steps turn Done by themselves once the data exists.',
                'Open Awaiting approval and press the arrow on each line to approve what others have proposed.',
                'As an administrator, press the gold tick (Mark as done) on Review IFRS 9 reports & data quality and Management sign-off for the period when they are complete.',
                'Open Team messages, type a note for colleagues and press Send.',
            ],
            'images' => [
                'workspace' => 'The Workspace: the period selector, the four tiles and the ten-step close checklist with System, Done and Pending badges',
                'workspace-approvals' => 'The Awaiting approval tab: each line counts what waits for a second person and links to the screen where it is approved',
            ],
            'routes' => ['workspace.index'],
        ],

        'Notifications' => [
            'body' => '<p>The bell in the top bar, to the left of your avatar, is your in-system notice board. The platform writes a notification to it when something concerns you: a ticket you raised or were assigned is created, changed or commented on, or another administrator ticks or reopens a manual step of the Workspace checklist. These events are not emailed; the bell is the only channel, so glance at it when you sign in. Every signed-in user has a bell and sees only their own notifications.</p>'
                . '<h4>What you see on the screen</h4><ul>'
                . '<li><b>The bell</b>: grey on white when there is nothing unread. With unread notifications it turns amber, swings gently every few seconds and carries a red badge with the number unread (<b>9+</b> beyond nine). The count is refreshed every time you open another page.</li>'
                . '<li><b>The panel</b> (press the bell): headed <b>Notifications</b>, with a green <b>Mark all read</b> link on the right while anything is unread.</li>'
                . '<li><b>The list</b>: your eight most recent notifications, newest first. Each row has a dot (green for unread, grey for read), the message and a relative time such as <b>2 hours ago</b>; hover the time for the full date and time. Unread rows have a pale green background.</li></ul>'
                . '<h4>Which events raise a notification</h4><ul>'
                . '<li><b>Ticket #012 created:</b> and the title: sent to the person the new ticket is assigned to.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Ticket #012 updated (In Progress):</b> and the title: sent to the assignee and the creator when its details or status are edited.</li>'
                . '<li><b>New update on ticket #012:</b> and the first 80 characters of the note: sent to the assignee and the creator when a progress note is posted.</li>'
                . '<li>A name followed by <b>completed "Review IFRS 9 reports &amp; data quality" for 2025-11.</b> (or <b>reopened</b>): sent to every other administrator when a manual Workspace step is ticked or reopened.</li></ul>'
                . '<p>You are never notified of your own action; only the other people involved are. Each notification links to the page it concerns.</p>'
                . '<h4>Buttons and icons</h4><ul><li><b>Bell</b>: opens or closes the panel and loads the latest list.</li><li><b>A notification row</b>: marks it read and opens the ticket or Workspace page it refers to.</li><li><b>Mark all read</b>: marks every notification read and clears the badge.</li><li>Pressing anywhere outside the panel closes it.</li></ul>'
                . '<h4>To read and clear notifications</h4><ol><li>Press the bell.</li><li>Press a row to open what it refers to; the row is marked read and the badge drops by one.</li><li>Press <b>Mark all read</b> to clear the badge without opening each item.</li></ol>'
                . '<h4>What happens next</h4><p>Marking a notification read changes only its dot and the badge; it stays in your list. The badge is recalculated by the server on every page load, so if a colleague acts while you are reading, the new count appears on your next click.</p>'
                . '<h4>Empty states and messages</h4><ul><li><b>Loading notifications...</b> while the list loads.</li><li><b>No notifications yet.</b> when you have never received one.</li></ul>'
                . '<h4>Common problems</h4><ul><li><b>The bell never changes.</b> Nothing has been assigned to you and you do not hold the administrator role. Ask to be the assignee on tickets you should follow.</li><li><b>The list is empty but the badge shows a number.</b> Press the bell again to reload the list; if it persists, refresh the page.</li><li><b>I expected an email.</b> Platform events are bell only. The system emails only login details to new users and password reset links.</li><li><b>Approvals are not notified.</b> Items waiting for a second person are not sent to the bell; they are listed on the Workspace, Awaiting approval tab.</li></ul>',
            'steps' => [
                'Look at the bell in the top bar: amber with a red number means you have unread notifications.',
                'Press the bell to open the Notifications panel.',
                'Press a notification to go to the ticket or Workspace page it concerns; it is marked read.',
                'Press Mark all read to clear the badge in one go.',
                'Press anywhere outside the panel to close it.',
            ],
            'images' => ['dashboard' => 'The notification bell sits in the top bar, to the left of the avatar'],
        ],

        'Support tickets' => [
            'body' => '<p>Support Tickets is the register of every enhancement request, issue and change request raised on the platform, shared by MAIIC and the developer. Each ticket carries a unique reference such as <b>#012</b>, a category, a priority, a status, an assignee and a full activity trail, so both sides can see what was asked, who is doing it and where it stands. Reading the register needs the <code>tickets.index</code> permission; creating, updating and deleting need <code>tickets.create</code>, <code>tickets.update</code> and <code>tickets.destroy</code>. To reach it, open <b>Administration &amp; support</b>, then <b>Support &amp; Maintenance</b>, then <b>Support Tickets</b>.</p>'
                . '<h4>What you see on the screen</h4><ul>'
                . '<li>Title <b>Support Tickets</b> and the line <b>Log and follow enhancement requests, issues and change requests for the system</b>.</li>'
                . '<li><b>New ticket</b> (green, plus icon) in the actions row above the table.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Status tabs</b>, each with the real count: <b>All</b>, <b>Open</b>, <b>In progress</b>, <b>Resolved</b>, <b>Closed</b>. The chosen tab is green.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Filter row</b>: a search box <b>Search reference or title</b> (it also matches the Requested by name), a drop-down <b>All categories</b> (Enhancement, Issue, Change Request, Other) and a <b>Clear</b> link once anything is set.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Table columns</b>: <b>Ref</b> (green, monospaced, a link), <b>Title</b> (a link), <b>Category</b>, <b>Priority</b>, <b>Status</b>, <b>Assigned to</b>, <b>Updated</b> and <b>Actions</b>. Fifteen tickets a page with numbered pages below.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Badge colours</b>. Status: <b>Open</b> gold, <b>In Progress</b> green, <b>On Hold</b> grey, <b>Resolved</b> solid green, <b>Closed</b> grey. Priority: <b>Low</b> grey, <b>Medium</b> green, <b>High</b> gold, <b>Critical</b> red. Category: <b>Enhancement</b> green, <b>Issue</b> red, <b>Change Request</b> gold, <b>Other</b> grey.</li></ul>'
                . '<h4>Buttons and icons</h4><ul>'
                . '<li><b>New ticket</b>: opens the New ticket form. Needs <code>tickets.create</code>.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Green eye</b> (<b>View</b>): opens the ticket.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Gold pencil</b> (<b>Edit</b>): opens the ticket with the Details card already in edit mode. Needs <code>tickets.update</code>.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Red bin</b> (<b>Delete</b>): asks <b>Delete ticket #012?</b> with <b>The ticket and its activity trail are removed for good.</b>; press <b>Delete ticket</b> to confirm or <b>Cancel</b>. Needs <code>tickets.destroy</code>.</li></ul>'
                . '<h4>The New ticket form</h4><p>Title <b>New ticket</b>, a <b>Back to tickets</b> button, and the line <b>Will be logged as #012</b> (the next number). Two sections:</p><ul>'
                . '<li><b>The request</b>: <b>Title</b> (required, up to 255 characters; prompt <b>Short summary of the request</b>), <b>Description</b> (prompt <b>Details, context and what done looks like</b>), <b>Category</b> (Enhancement by default), <b>Priority</b> (Medium by default) and <b>Status</b> (Open by default).</li>'
                . '<li><b>Who and when</b>: <b>Requested by</b> (for example <b>Finance team</b>), <b>Source</b> (for example email, meeting or phone; up to 40 characters), <b>Assign to</b> (<b>Unassigned</b> or any user) and <b>Due date</b>.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Cancel</b> returns to the list; <b>Create ticket</b> (tick icon) saves and reads <b>Saving...</b> meanwhile.</li></ul>'
                . '<h4>The ticket page</h4><ul>'
                . '<li>Heading: the reference and title, with <b>Logged</b> the date <b>by</b> the creator <b>; the activity below is the full trail</b>. In the actions row: <b>Delete</b> (red outline, bin icon; needs <code>tickets.destroy</code>) and <b>Back to tickets</b>.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Description</b> card (or <b>No description provided.</b>), with a green <b>Resolution</b> box once a resolution is written.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Activity</b>: a timeline. Grey dots are system entries such as <b>Ticket logged.</b>; green dots are notes by people. A status change shows the old and new status badges; every entry carries the author and the date and time. Empty: <b>No activity yet.</b></li>'
                . '<li><b>Add an update</b> (needs <code>tickets.update</code>): a box with the prompt <b>Progress note, comment or resolution detail</b>, a <b>Change status to</b> drop-down whose first option is <b>keep</b> and the current status, and <b>Post update</b>.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Details</b> card with the rows <b>Status</b>, <b>Category</b>, <b>Priority</b>, <b>Assignee</b>, <b>Requested by</b>, <b>Source</b>, <b>Due</b>, <b>Created</b> and, once set, <b>Resolved</b>. The gold <b>Edit</b> button (pencil; needs <code>tickets.update</code>) turns the card into a form with <b>Title</b>, <b>Description</b>, <b>Status</b>, <b>Category</b>, <b>Priority</b>, <b>Assignee</b>, <b>Requested by</b>, <b>Source</b>, <b>Due date</b>, <b>Resolution</b> and <b>Save changes</b>; the button becomes <b>Cancel</b>.</li></ul>'
                . '<h4>To raise a ticket</h4><ol><li>Press <b>New ticket</b>.</li><li>Type a clear <b>Title</b> and a <b>Description</b> of what is needed.</li><li>Choose the category, priority and status, then fill <b>Requested by</b>, <b>Source</b>, <b>Assign to</b> and <b>Due date</b> as needed.</li><li>Press <b>Create ticket</b>. The ticket page opens with <b>Ticket logged.</b> in its activity.</li></ol>'
                . '<h4>To add a progress note or change the status</h4><ol><li>Open the ticket (green eye, or press its reference).</li><li>Type the note under <b>Add an update</b> (required, up to 5,000 characters).</li><li>Leave <b>Change status to</b> on <b>keep</b>, or choose the new status.</li><li>Press <b>Post update</b>.</li></ol>'
                . '<h4>What happens next</h4><p>Creating a ticket writes the first activity entry and shows <b>Ticket #012 created successfully.</b> Editing shows <b>Ticket #012 updated.</b>; a note shows <b>Update added to #012.</b>; deleting returns to the list with <b>Ticket #012 deleted.</b> Moving a ticket to Resolved or Closed stamps the <b>Resolved</b> date. Every create, update, note and delete is written to the Audit Trail (<b>Create Ticket #012</b>, <b>Update Ticket #012</b>, <b>Comment on Ticket #012</b>, <b>Delete Ticket #012</b>) and sends a bell notification to the assignee and the creator, other than the person acting. References are never reused.</p>'
                . '<h4>Empty states and messages</h4><ul><li><b>No tickets here</b> with <b>Log a request or a problem with New ticket.</b>, or with <b>Nothing matches these filters. Clear them to see every ticket.</b> when a filter is set.</li></ul>'
                . '<h4>Common problems</h4><ul><li><b>New ticket, the pencil or the bin is missing.</b> Your role lacks the create, update or delete permission for tickets.</li><li><b>The title field is required.</b> Enter a title before pressing <b>Create ticket</b>.</li><li><b>The source must not be greater than 40 characters.</b> Shorten Source.</li><li><b>The body field is required.</b> A progress note cannot be empty.</li><li><b>I cannot find a ticket.</b> Press <b>All</b> and <b>Clear</b>, then search by the reference number.</li></ul>',
            'steps' => [
                'Open Administration & support, then Support & Maintenance, then Support Tickets.',
                'Press New ticket and note the reference shown after Will be logged as.',
                'Type a clear Title and a Description of what is needed and what done looks like.',
                'Choose Category, Priority and Status; fill Requested by, Source, Assign to and Due date.',
                'Press Create ticket. The ticket page opens with Ticket logged. in its Activity.',
                'To report progress, open the ticket, type under Add an update, choose Change status to if the status moves, and press Post update.',
            ],
            'images' => [
                'tickets' => 'The Support Tickets register: status tabs with counts, search and category filter, the badges and the row icons',
                'tickets-create' => 'The New ticket form with its reference, The request and Who and when sections',
            ],
            'routes' => ['tickets.index', 'tickets.create', 'tickets.show'],
        ],
    ],
];
